; MAC-LANG-17's one refusal (AX3066).
;
; A `(literals ...)` header reserves its members: an occurrence
; stops binding and matches one binding instead. A member no
; pattern spells is therefore dead text - and the likeliest reading
; is a typo for a name the patterns spell, in which case the rule
; binds where the author meant to match. `ghost` below is that
; typo: the rules spell `+`, never `ghost`.
(macro haunted (literals + ghost)
  ((haunted (+ a b))
   (:: summing (-> Int Int Int))
   (fn (summing x y) (+ x y)))
  ((haunted other)
   (:: stray Int)
   (fn (stray) 0)))

(haunted (+ 1 2))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (summing 1 2))
